WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:03.270
(jazz music)

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.860
- [Kenny] This is a review
of the best styluses,

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.690
for the most popular tablets.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:11.500
- The plural of stylus is actually styli.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.430
- What do you know? You're
not even wearing pants.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.302
- You dressed me, you foo--

00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:17.660
(gentle music)

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.860
- [Kenny] If you're looking to cartoon,

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.170
take notes or design,
you've got lots of options.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.560
Every year, tech companies
pitch their stylus,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.910
and tablet combos with varying degrees,

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.412
of rhetorical flourish.

00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:29.860
- [Woman] Our fastest S Pen yet.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.160
- Game changing accessory.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:32.220
- So I really love this pen.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.960
- Which basically all
amount to them just saying,

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.950
buy our stick.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.930
So I set out to find the
best tablet stylus combo,

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.600
for mixed use with an emphasis on drawing.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.840
Tested tablets included the big three.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.440
A 12.9" inch Apple iPad Pro.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.460
The Microsoft Surface Pro 8.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.320
And a Samsung Galaxy Tab S8+.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.810
I tested styluses for all three devices.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.800
Sadly, you can't mix and match.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.890
So no Apple Pencil on a Galaxy tab,

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.660
or Samsung S Pen with a Microsoft Surface.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.700
But I did throw in some
leading third party options,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.533
for the iPad,

00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:06.680
since it currently holds the
tablet market share throne.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.270
All styluses were evaluated,

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.340
on a few core pieces of criteria.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.970
Built-in comfort, pressure
sensitivity and ink flow,

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:15.840
and software options.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.610
First, let's take a look
at the styluses themselves.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:21.180
Look. As a kid, I collected pens.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.020
- Nerd.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:22.853
- [Kenny] As such,

00:01:22.853 --> 00:01:26.350
I'm snobby about the feel
and weightiness of a stylus.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.420
When it comes to the
best in-hand experience,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:32.060
it's a horse race between
the $129 Apple Pencil 2,

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.890
and the $119 Microsoft Surface Slim Pen 2.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.650
Both feel great, are easy
to use for long sessions,

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:40.830
have magnetic docking mechanisms,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.500
and sturdy tactile replaceable nibs.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.620
Which you can replace for around $20.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:47.550
Where the Surface Slim Pen inches ahead,

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.350
is with its more pointed
nib and haptic feedback.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:51.920
The Slim Pen vibrates lightly,

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.010
to emulate the feel of real paper.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.660
It takes a second to get
used to but it's pleasant.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.270
For a similar experience on the iPad,

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.500
with the Apple Pencil 2,

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.620
I had to purchase a $40
screen protector by Paperlike,

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.393
which adds friction and resistance,

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.390
but like all screen protectors,
is a pain to put on.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.150
Samsung's $60 S Pen.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.970
Though innovative with its soft nibs,

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.410
feels too insubstantial.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:17.700
Like something you get to
keep score at putt-putt.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.300
Also the nibs wear down quickly,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.750
and Samsung does not offer replacements.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.230
For a larger S Pen experience,

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:26.210
you can upgrade to the $100 S Pen Pro.

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:27.820
As for the third party options,

00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:29.650
I like the feel of the $70 Zagg.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.563
It's basically a clone size
wise of the Apple Pencil 2.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.220
And the Logitech Crayon feels solid,

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.300
but looks like a relative
to the pencil Steve used,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.710
in "Blue's Clues".

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:40.710
(gentle music)

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.240
Meanwhile, the Adonit
Note+ could be better.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.010
It feels like something
you could buy with tickets,

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:46.023
at a mall arcade.

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:48.730
And one quick note when stylus shopping,

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:49.950
choose one with a flat edge,

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.320
or one that resembles
a carpenter's pencil.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.070
Fully circular styluses will
roll off your couch or desk,

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.540
into some other abyss.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.080
For me, the winner for design is a tie,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:02.510
between the Apple Pencil 2
and the Surface Slim Pen 2.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.580
The best budget and note
taking option goes to the Zagg.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.810
Next, let's talk about
pressure sensitivity,

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.230
and palm rejection.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.330
When it comes to illustrating,

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.160
pressure sensitivity is paramount.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.140
Especially for pressure
sensitive brush types,

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.100
and smooth line transitions.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.960
Only some of the styluses tested,

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.710
supported pressure sensitivity.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:23.400
Those with the feature are the
Apple Pencil Gen 1 and Gen 2,

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:27.040
the Microsoft Surface Slim
Pen 2, the Samsung S Pen,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.250
and the Adonit Note+.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.070
I'm including the Apple Pencil Gen 1 here,

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.840
because the $329 entry level iPad,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.810
only supports the Apple Pencil 1.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.960
For drawing, I preferred
the fine pointed tips,

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.140
on the Apple Pencil 2 and
Microsoft Surface Slim Pen 2,

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:46.900
which offer more of a
pen to paper experience.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.730
While the S Pen is the most responsive,

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.730
of any of the options in its own app,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.500
it didn't perform
consistently across all apps.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.910
Plus the S Pen nib feels a bit
more like a Sharpie marker.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:04:00.040
And while the Adonit Note+
does have pressure sensitivity,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.210
it's spotty at best and
nonfunctional at worst.

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:05.503
This is what happens
when you try to connect,

00:04:05.503 --> 00:04:07.933
the Adonit to Procreate.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.350
Non-stylus. No.

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:14.670
An Adonit spokeswoman told me,

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:17.770
this is due to Procreate currently
not supporting the Note+.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:18.790
And then there are the styluses,

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.600
without pressure sensitivity.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.910
These are the options more suited,

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.820
for handwriting and note taking.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.610
On that front, the Zagg led the way,

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:28.370
with the Logitech Crayon 2 close behind.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.860
The top choices too all
fared incredibly well,

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.040
when it came to palm rejection.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.480
Maybe one little error mark there.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.100
Overall, the Apple
Pencil 2 just edged out,

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.200
the Microsoft Surface Slim Pen 2.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.130
Apple's option is slightly more sensitive,

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.960
to delicate line strokes.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.490
And if you're not looking to draw as much,

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.660
the budget pick, again, goes to the Zagg.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.480
Lastly, a stylus is only as good,

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.930
as the operating system
and apps it works with.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:55.790
Between Windows, Android
and iOS app stores,

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.590
there are dozens of sketching,
illustrating, design,

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:00.320
and note taking apps.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.740
After trying some of the top ones,

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.300
I couldn't shake my love for Procreate.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.700
Which is available only
for iPad OS for $10.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.410
The level of control and customization,

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.170
with the Apple Pencil on
Procreate is not only nuanced,

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.180
but easy to use, which
for someone like me,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:17.150
who doesn't draw full
time, is very important.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:19.640
And you can cheat by making
straight lines and shapes,

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.250
which I do pretty often.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.857
- So you can't even draw a circle.

00:05:23.857 --> 00:05:26.120
- [Kenny] And you can also
export your Procreate projects,

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.970
into Photoshop format
and keep all your layers.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.170
Sadly, Procreate isn't available
for Windows or Android,

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:33.900
nor are there any current plans,

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.070
for it to be developed for them,

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:37.180
according to a Procreate spokeswoman.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.780
I did, however, like
Sketchable for Windows,

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.440
which offers a similar
degree of accessibility,

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.180
Photoshop exporting, and
layered functionality.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:48.210
For pros, Adobe's 9.99
per month Photoshop,

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:51.500
is available on both the
iPad and Surface Pro.

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.370
For note takers, all the
tablets include free apps.

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.743
Apple has Notes. Samsung has Notes.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:05:59.680
And Microsoft has OneNote.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.170
By far the beefiest most powerful option.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.530
I prefer GoodNotes, an iPad only option,

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.470
just because of how easy
it is to search notes.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.530
So what should you get?

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.680
I would get the Apple Pencil
2 and any of the new iPads.

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.750
But the competition is creeping
up on Apple, and quick.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.520
I love the Microsoft Surface experience,

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:19.830
with the Slim Pen 2 and its
very fine and pointy tip.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.710
And the super responsive
low latency Sharpie style,

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:25.260
on the S Pen was awfully
fun to write with.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.800
- Is that supposed to be a mustache?

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.243
- It definitely is.

